Third-party code and data keep their own licences:
- src/battery_twin/_vendor/blast_lite: NREL BLAST-Lite, BSD-3-Clause (see its LICENSE and NOTICE).
- src/battery_twin/data/kirkaldy2024: Kirkaldy et al. (2024) dataset, CC-BY-4.0.
- src/battery_twin/data/published_ageing.csv: values read from the figures and text of
  Preger et al. 2020, Wittman et al. 2023, Ohneseit et al. 2025 and Luh & Blank 2024
  (see the file and the Sources tab); credit and licences belong to those publications.
- src/battery_twin/data/severson2019_cycle_life.csv: Severson et al., Nature Energy 4,
  383 (2019), Supplementary Table 9.
- Every other file and folder in src/battery_twin/data/ states its source and licence in
  its README.md; README section 14 lists them all. Most are CC BY 4.0. The MIT licence
  above does not cover them. In particular src/battery_twin/data/popp2024 (University of
  Wuppertal, Samsung 50E) is for non-commercial use only, and src/battery_twin/data/lam2024
  has no stated licence (derived values, kept with attribution).
